Quick care reminders for Pothos:
- Light: bright, indirect light ideal; tolerates low light (avoid direct hot sun).  
- Water: let the top 1–2 inches of soil dry between waterings; don’t let the plant sit in water.  
- Soil & pot: well-draining potting mix and a pot with drainage holes.  
- Temperature & humidity: 65–85°F (18–29°C); average home humidity is OK, higher humidity helps.  
- Feeding: balanced houseplant fertilizer monthly during spring/summer.  
- Pruning & propagation: prune to control length and encourage bushiness; cuttings root easily in water or soil.  
- Pets: toxic if ingested — keep out of reach of pets and children.

